      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stem%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Cozart‑Coley House, a preserved antebellum home, sits in Stem and is a key landmark of the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stem%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Stem’s first fire station, now the town hall and police department, was built thanks to a community fundraising effort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stemnc.org/about-stem/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s origin traces back to the area known as Tally Ho, a name that also inspired a local tavern’s fox‑hunting call.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
